## Scientific And Domain Assessments

### Inherited exact-synonym applicability: Aquakay

identity: supported. Targets: menadione-aquakay.

same-substance chemical synonym. Retain the sourced conventional menadione chemical-name sense for coordinator/W01 consideration. Brand annotation alone is not grounds to reject it. Do not treat an Aquakay finished dosage product as neat menadione.

Historical FDA listings identify Aquakay tablets/injection but do not establish their complete composition. No claim of universal brand identity, historical formulation equality, all-country/all-time coverage, owner admission or export clearance.

### Inherited exact-synonym applicability: Aquinone

identity: supported. Targets: menadione-aquinone.

same-substance chemical synonym. Retain the supported conventional substance-name sense for coordinator/W01 consideration. Do not infer the complete identity of historical Aquinone Bischoff Injection from chemical databases or from its product name.

The historical product listing does not specify a salt, solvent, concentration or complete formulation. Absence of these details is not grounds to reject the demonstrated chemical synonym. No guessed derivative, historical formulation equivalence or global row/export approval.

### Inherited exact-synonym applicability: Hemodal

identity: concern. Targets: menadione-hemodal.

nonresolving source label justified. Withhold unqualified exact resolution of the inherited bare Hemodal token pending contextual reconciliation. A provenance-preserving nonresolving disposition is scientifically justified for this unqualified inherited entry; retain its raw spelling/source/history and positive conventional chemical usage. Root/W01 decide the native representation and any change after filing/review.

This does not mean every Hemodal use is false or that the positive database association should be erased. No replacement identity/CURIE, derivative structure, formulation-wide component inference or quantity extrapolation is proposed. The original kg_microbe token lacks a product/date/context selector.

### Inherited exact-synonym applicability: Kappaxin

identity: supported. Targets: menadione-kappaxin.

same-substance chemical synonym. Retain supported conventional menadione chemical-name use. Preserve the distinct historical Kappaxin injection boundary; do not resolve whole finished injection to neat compound.

No inferred solvent, salt, dose, purity or current marketed status. Positive chemical-name evidence is not generic approval of every historical Kappaxin product or the entire owner row.

### Before/after, history and source boundaries

provenance: supported. Targets: menadione-aquakay, menadione-aquinone, menadione-hemodal, menadione-kappaxin.

Four tokens unchanged; W08 only adds the separate ATCC compound-name context. All original holds and source versions remain.

## Findings

### MENADIONE-HEMODAL-001: Bare inherited Hemodal spans documented distinct chemical materials

major / open / confirmed; issue key: menadione-inherited-hemodal-material-ambiguity.

Bayer historical tablet and bisulfite injection descriptions, reinforced by the manufacturer neutral/bisulfite synonym collision, show actual chemical-scope ambiguity. Positive neutral-menadione name association remains valid in context. The unqualified inherited EXACT_SYNONYM requires coordinator reconciliation; this is not a blanket assertion that all Hemodal usage is false.

## Recommended Actions And Acceptance Checks

### root-hemodal-triage

Root/W01 reconcile the inherited Hemodal entry using claim-specific primary evidence; preserve its text/history and neutral-use association while selecting any future nonresolving representation. No fix is performed by this packet.

- Retain exact source text/history and positive chemical-name association.
- Do not map the historical derivative/injection to neutral menadione or guess a replacement identity.
- Any future changed complete owner/row receives required independent review; no admission from this research packet.

